We do NOT care about individual train sequences. //uses greedy + two pointer
We only care about how many trains are present at the station at the same time.

So the goal becomes:

Find the maximum number of overlapping time interval
platforms needed = number of active trains
Arrival → +1 active train
Departure → -1 active train

We track the maximum value reached.

class Solution {
    public int minPlatform(int arr[], int dep[]) {
        //  code here
        Arrays.sort(arr);
        Arrays.sort(dep);
        int i = 0;
        int j = 0;
        int count = 0;
        int max = 0;
        while(i < arr.length && j < dep.length){
            if(arr[i] <= dep[j]){
                count++;
                max = Math.max(count,max);
                i++;
            } 
            else{
                count--;
                j++;
            }
        }
        return max;
    }
}
